<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beckman Revolt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1684">1684</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Beckman Revolt was a settlers' rising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a>, capital of the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a>, in February 1684, led by the planter Manuel Beckman. The rebels expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>, who opposed the enslavement of indigenous people, and abolished the trading company that held a monopoly on the supply of enslaved Africans and goods. A new governor restored order in 1685, and Beckman was hanged.</p></div>
